{
  "id": "mit",
  "term": "MIT",
  "definition": "MIT, or motor imagery training, is a cognitive method in which a person mentally practices a specific movement without actually producing the movement. In psychology and motor research, it is used as a task-focused form of mental rehearsal that engages brain pathways similar to those involved in carrying out the action itself.",
